        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-18T14:01:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have done a thorough analysis of those, but at host it is very early boot and MMU might not be even there and I am not sure if that would work.\n\nstacktrace is used at panics so it doesn\u0027t make to run debug code in there.\n\nserial is typically used for debugging, which can be called very early also.",
      "parentUuid": "02eed020_c0742183",
      "revId": "09fbdb92acebadde2b9c6df3d1a7b9a7b7296144",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d053704_7313722c",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/Makefile",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T09:26:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what we gain with filtering out stuff that aren\u0027t using hyp_alloc. That\u0027s quite cumbersome and if later we add hyp_alloc() in there we won\u0027t see it.\n\nAlso, host is an assembly file, I\u0027m not sure the instrumentation applies there. Is it really worth it?\n\nFair enough for stacktrace and setup. And actually I have removed them from FTRACE as well, but that\u0027s really disputable. I think I didn\u0027t want to take the risk of messing-up with stacktrace.\n\nSerial though I would really just keep it out. Otherwise we create precedent of handling a list of files that are debug option. Ftrace is one of them and you haven\u0027t added to the list.\n\nOverall I am still not convinced \"host\" and \"serial\" make sense.",
      "parentUuid": "2e0e1686_064eb3b3",
      "revId": "09fbdb92acebadde2b9c6df3d1a7b9a7b7296144",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
